# Finish work with a commit

When a work session makes repository changes and reaches a completed or handoff-ready stopping point:

- Commit all intended changes on the current task branch before the final report.
- Push the commit so reviewers and automations can observe the new SHA.
- In the final report, state the pushed commit SHA and the exact checks/tests run.
- If the session made no repository changes, explicitly report: `no changes / no commit`.
- Do not leave completed changes only in the working tree.
- Do not commit unrelated pre-existing user changes.
- Do not create a replacement/duplicate PR merely to satisfy this rule; continue on the assigned branch/PR unless the task explicitly requires a separate repository or scope.
